## 16. Contested shot message and goalie late-intercept fallback (2026-11-14)

- Added `SHOT_CONTESTED`: the challenger keeps executing its active shot, but estimates whether the nearest opponent can reach the predicted contact point at least 0.15s before its own intercept. It broadcasts the expected contact time instead of abandoning the shot.
- The race estimate uses the active routine's `intercept_time` and corresponding predicted ball slice; for `short_shot`, which has no predicted intercept, it compares ETAs to the current ball. Opponent ETA uses distance, facing, horizontal speed and height.
- Only the elected goalie reacts to `SHOT_CONTESTED`, and only while the ball is in our half (`ball_depth > 0`). The message carries both the challenger's expected contact time and the estimated opponent contact ETA. The goalie holds its goal-side `goalie_followup_wait` position until 0.10s after the opponent's estimated touch (or the challenger's contact time if no opponent ETA is available), then calls `fast_intercept_finder.find` with that later earliest time to select the first reachable follow-up touch from the refreshed ball prediction.
