- In 2v2/3v3, if the deepest player is also elected challenger due to its facing angle, the next-deepest teammate is promoted to goalie so the fallback is always a different car.
- The 3v3 transition player does not treat `SHOT_CONTESTED` as a normal offensive shot announcement; its existing transition behaviour remains separate.
- This uses the existing `goalie_followup_wait` and `fast_intercept_finder` routines. The opponent ETA is an approximation, not a full opponent physics simulation. No compile or in-game test has been run.

## 17. Party Cannon JumpShot reference (pinned commit)

- Source: `RedUtils/Actions/JumpShot.cs` at `ea84e4325ddb60565bbac6fb9766dc45f38b58cb`.
- It predicts the post-hit ball velocity and travel time toward the target, derives a shot direction, places the car target about 165 units behind the ball along that direction, adjusts for surface normal/jump height, then subtracts another 25 units of horizontal shot direction for contact power/reliability.
- It updates target and shot direction every 0.2s while approaching with a timed `Arrive` action. It only jumps when the predicted jump position is within roughly 50 units of the target and the remaining time matches the required jump time.
- In the air it aims along `DodgeDirection`, rolls its roof away from the dodge direction relative to the contact surface, holds jump until close to contact, releases for at least three frames, then dodges in the flattened shot direction about 0.05s before contact.
- The timed `Arrive` creates `Drive(..., wasteBoost: true)`; boost is still gated by required target speed, forward alignment and speed. The jump-shot's airborne phase itself does not continuously boost.
- Party Cannon uses `BoostAccel=991.667`, `BoostConsumption=33.3/s`, `AirThrottleAccel=66.667`, and `MaxSpeed=2300`. Its ETA model assumes the available boost can be spent to reach maximum speed; it does not enforce a fixed reserve for every action.


## 18. Party Cannon JumpShot and boost-management port (2026-11-14)

- Replaced the live `jump_shot` class in `routines of volt` with a Party Cannon-derived implementation, pinned to `ea84e4325ddb60565bbac6fb9766dc45f38b58cb`.
